{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>For [You have forsaken].</b> Some say that the tav of נטשתה is second person to HaShem, and the meaning is that the prophet gives thanks to HaShem that in truth He forsook them, for they were filled from the east. R. Moses the Cohen said that the tav of the second person is to Israel, and the meaning is: You have forgotten Your people and His Torah." "<b>For they are filled.</b> Some say: they went mad, like קראו אחריך מלא (Isaiah 9:11). The correct view in my eyes is that they are filled with the wisdom of the children of the east, and they are Aram; thus he wrote: Aram from the east and Philistines from behind, therefore as before and so again; and so ughafter; and the house of Jacob will be in the manner of an appellation, as in the first [comment]." "<b>And with the children of foreigners they abound.</b> What thought has produced, for the middle term between two combined propositions is called 'born,' and ישפיקו is like אם ישפוק עפר שמרון (1 Kings 20:10). And if they are two hitpa'el forms, the meaning is that they have enough with external wisdoms and do not seek prophecy, which is the light."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:51:38.757081732Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}